{"id":"swale_similarity","title":"SWALE rewards and gap costs","family":"elastic","definition":"reference","intro_en":"SWALE scores tolerance-based matches with a reward and unmatched observations with a gap penalty. Its recurrence combines the number of accepted matches with the price of omitted observations. This example uses reward 2, gap score -0.5 and epsilon 0.35; the raw score is not normalized to a probability.","intro_zh":"SWALE 对容差内的匹配给奖励，对未匹配的观测施加间隙惩罚。递推同时考虑接受的匹配数量与省略观测的费用。本例奖励为 2、间隙分数为 -0.5、容差为 0.35；原始分数没有归一化为概率。","steps_en":["Set the stated local scoring rule, tolerance and boundary conditions.","Reward a tolerance match; otherwise choose the less costly gap transition.","Trace the selected predecessor operations from the complete-prefix state.","Read the final score with the normalization explicitly stated below."],"steps_zh":["设置明确的局部计分规则、容差与边界条件。","对容差匹配给予奖励，否则选择费用较低的间隙转移。","从完整前缀状态沿选定的前驱操作回溯。","按下方明确的归一化约定读取最终分数。"],"formula":"S_ij=2+S_(i-1,j-1) for a tolerance match; otherwise max(S_(i-1,j)-0.5,S_(i,j-1)-0.5)","caveats_en":["Rewards, gap penalties and sequence length influence the score scale. This implements the paper's scoring recurrence, not its FTSE acceleration.","The small arrays are an algorithm illustration, not evidence of retrieval or classification quality."],"caveats_zh":["奖励、间隙惩罚和序列长度都会影响分数量级；本例演示论文的计分递推，没有实现 FTSE 加速。","这些小数组用于解释计算过程，不构成检索或分类性能证据。"],"sources":[{"label":"Morse and Patel (2007), Definition 5.1","url":"https://dbgroup.eecs.umich.edu/files/sigmod07timeseries.pdf"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"normalization":"none","local_norm":"absolute difference","epsilon":0.35,"match_reward":2.0,"gap_score":-0.5},"result":{"label":"alignment score","value":17.0,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compare samples to construc